  "disposition": {
    "confirmed": "The focused03 test and concurrent build share dist/web incompatibly: the test installs a persistent HTML fixture there and Vite explicitly clears that directory at renderStart.",
    "supportedFailureMechanism": "Deletion or replacement of the fixture during the final case can select the production index fallback or temporary 503 instead of the fixture, leaving the expected alert absent. The build overlapped that case and wrote index/assets during it.",
    "unobserved": "No failing navigation response body, browser trace, request timestamp or unlink event was retained; the exact response and unique cause of the timeout are not established.",
    "serialValidation": "Focused04 ran the same 24 files/options/deadlines alone after the completed build and passed 334 with three explicit Windows skips. All four plugin-frame cases passed.",
    "attribution": "No concrete M15 runtime defect was identified. This is not a claim that the failure occurred on an executed baseline. Focused03 remains FAIL."
  },
  "commandsEqualExceptResultDestination": true,
  "testTimeoutMs": 60000,
  "confirmedSourceMechanism": {
    "fixtureCreation": "tests/plugin-frame-custody.test.ts beforeAll creates dist/web/plugin-custody-${randomUUID()}.html once. Cases 1 and 4 load it; cases 2 and 3 load server-defined unrestricted routes.",
    "build": "scripts/build.mjs starts Vite build; vite.config.ts sets root apps/web, outDir ../../dist/web, emptyOutDir true.",
    "cleanup": "Installed Vite 7.3.7 prepareOutDirPlugin renderStart order pre calls prepareOutDir, whose emptyDir removes files recursively. The fixture has no exclusion.",
    "serverFallback": "apps/server/server.ts wildcard route maps missing files to dist/web/index.html and returns 503 if the fallback cannot be read.",
    "cssBoundary": "The plugin-frame test esbuild bundle helper sets loader .css to empty. The two CSS changes after focused02 do not execute in those test bundles."
  },
